Q: How can I build a separate main.css file from src/styles that doesn&#39;t get bundled with page specific css files? A: <p>Astro already does CSS chunking: page CSS is split per-route, and shared CSS is extracted for reuse.</p>
<p>What looks like “duplication” is actually small CSS being <em>inlined</em> per page (default behaviour).</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>// astro.config.mjs
import { defineConfig } from &quot;astro/config&quot;;

export default defineConfig({
  build: {
    inlineStylesheets: &quot;never&quot;, // force external CSS files, no per-page inlining
  },
});
</code></pre>
<p>Keep your current import in layout:</p>
<pre class="lang-none prettyprint-override"><code>---
// src/layouts/MainLayout.astro
import &quot;../styles/main.css&quot;;
---
</code></pre>
